<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  service_roads.osm - the three service classes hanging off a residential street.

  Node block 14xx, way block 140xx. Own patch around 53.3380 N, 6.2800 W.

  Way 14000 "Beechwood Avenue" is an ordinary residential street with a sidewalk
  on both sides. Three service roads leave it at INTERIOR nodes, so each one
  splits the parent and produces a degree 3 node rather than a coincidence of way
  endpoints:

    way 14010  service=driveway       at node 1402
    way 14020  service=parking_aisle  at node 1403
    way 14030  service=alley          at node 1404

  The service=* subtag, not the highway tag, is what sets the width: build_profile()
  reads driveway_width, parking_aisle_width and alley_width, which default to
  3.0 m, 5.5 m and 3.5 m. A parking aisle is therefore the WIDEST of the three
  and a driveway the narrowest, which is the ordering a builder that ignored the
  subtag and used service_lane_width for all three would flatten. None of them
  carries a kerb, a gutter or a sidewalk. Each is where a vehicle crosses the
  parent street's footway, so each is where the kerb has to drop.

  The three carry different surface values on purpose. A driveway in concrete, a
  parking aisle in asphalt and an alley in setts are all ordinary tagging, and
  they make the material mix in an OBJ dump say which service road is which.

  Way 14020 has two segments so a parking aisle is not a single straight stub:
  it turns, which is the case a narrow profile with a gutter has to miter without
  pinching.

  Expected:
    * three degree 3 nodes, at 1402, 1403 and 1404
    * every edge of ways 14010, 14020 and 14030 has RoadType::Service and no
      Sidewalk, CurbFace, CurbTop or Gutter strip
    * their total widths are 3.0 m, 5.5 m and 3.5 m, so 14010 < 14030 < 14020
    * way 14010 carries MaterialId::Concrete lanes, 14020 Asphalt, 14030 whatever
      the surface table maps setts onto
-->
<osm version="0.6" generator="stratum-test-fixture">
  <bounds minlat="53.33770" minlon="-6.28210" maxlat="53.33840" maxlon="-6.27790"/>

  <node id="1401" version="1" lat="53.33800" lon="-6.28200"/>
  <node id="1402" version="1" lat="53.33800" lon="-6.28100"/>
  <node id="1403" version="1" lat="53.33800" lon="-6.28000"/>
  <node id="1404" version="1" lat="53.33800" lon="-6.27900"/>
  <node id="1405" version="1" lat="53.33800" lon="-6.27800"/>

  <node id="1411" version="1" lat="53.33820" lon="-6.28100"/>

  <node id="1421" version="1" lat="53.33780" lon="-6.28000"/>
  <node id="1422" version="1" lat="53.33780" lon="-6.27960"/>

  <node id="1431" version="1" lat="53.33830" lon="-6.27900"/>

  <way id="14000" version="1">
    <nd ref="1401"/>
    <nd ref="1402"/>
    <nd ref="1403"/>
    <nd ref="1404"/>
    <nd ref="1405"/>
    <tag k="highway" v="residential"/>
    <tag k="name" v="Beechwood Avenue"/>
    <tag k="lanes" v="2"/>
    <tag k="maxspeed" v="50"/>
    <tag k="surface" v="asphalt"/>
    <tag k="sidewalk" v="both"/>
  </way>

  <way id="14010" version="1">
    <nd ref="1402"/>
    <nd ref="1411"/>
    <tag k="highway" v="service"/>
    <tag k="service" v="driveway"/>
    <tag k="surface" v="concrete"/>
  </way>

  <way id="14020" version="1">
    <nd ref="1403"/>
    <nd ref="1421"/>
    <nd ref="1422"/>
    <tag k="highway" v="service"/>
    <tag k="service" v="parking_aisle"/>
    <tag k="surface" v="asphalt"/>
    <tag k="oneway" v="yes"/>
  </way>

  <way id="14030" version="1">
    <nd ref="1404"/>
    <nd ref="1431"/>
    <tag k="highway" v="service"/>
    <tag k="service" v="alley"/>
    <tag k="surface" v="sett"/>
    <tag k="name" v="Beechwood Lane"/>
  </way>
</osm>
